rachel: Quick heads-up — I ran the observability docs smoke and found a broken heatmap example link plus an outdated Node tracing-hook snippet. Opening a small PR to patch. :mag_right:

linkchecker-bot: link-scan: /console/observability/heatmaps/example -> 404. Also flagged: /docs/examples/js-tracehook-legacy -> 404.

rachel: The heatmap page references an SDK tracehook snippet that uses the old API `trace.getSpan()` which our Node SDK removed. Current snippet on page (JS):

```js
// old
const { Console } = require('@redwood/inference')
const client = new Console()
const span = trace.getSpan()
span.setAttribute('cost_ms', 12)
```

rachel: New SDK uses `trace.getSpanContext()` and the span API returns a `setAttribute` on the span object differently. Proposed replacement:

```js
// new
import { Console } from '@redwood/inference'
import { trace } from '@opentelemetry/api'
const client = new Console()
const span = trace.getSpanContext() // returns context object
// use helper to set attributes from context
client.tracing.setSpanAttributesFromContext(span, { cost_ms: 12 })
```

omar: hmm we should avoid making a library helper required in the docs. Instead show a tiny compat snippet that maps the old convenience call to the new explicit API so users can migrate easily. Example proposal:

```js
// compat shim for migration
function setCost(oldStyleSpan, cost) {
  if (oldStyleSpan && typeof oldStyleSpan.setAttribute === 'function') {
    oldStyleSpan.setAttribute('cost_ms', cost)
  } else if (oldStyleSpan && oldStyleSpan.traceId) {
    // assume this is a span context
    client.tracing.setSpanAttributesFromContext(oldStyleSpan, { cost_ms: cost })
  }
}
```

tony: also note: the heatmap example's cost aggregation code expects `cost_ms` as a numeric field in span attributes. update the dashboard snippet that computes percentiles to read `Number(span.attributes.cost_ms)` and guard for undefined.

rachel: I'll update the heatmap page to replace the broken link with the new example path (/console/observability/heatmap-examples) and add frontmatter redirect for the old URL. Add frontmatter block at top:

```
---
redirect_from:
  - /console/observability/heatmaps/example
---
```

linkchecker-bot: note: please also update internal links from tutorials which still catalog the old example path — I can emit a list of pages referencing it.

pr-bot: PR created: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/5201 title: "docs: heatmap example link + JS tracehook snippet migration (compat shim)". CI: link-check queued, docs-render smoke check included.

ivy: small ask — include a tiny screenshot of the heatmap widget after change (PNG) and a short line in the changelog: "Heatmap example: migrated Node tracing hook to new span context API; added compat shim."

omar: also add a one-liner in the Node SDK changelog page and a cross-ref to migration notes so customers searching for `getSpan()` hits the migration doc.

rachel: assigning reviewers (SDK docs + observability). Will merge after CI green and one quick pair review. Thanks! :sparkles:
